WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:06.230
Hunting down the greatest 
thief of our time: Lupin III.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.360
There's only one rule.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:20.080
Oh, wow. Looks like you're the center of 
attention in a troublesome game, Lupin.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.950
<b>Updates</b>

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:25.960
<b>Goemon's got such good posture!! 
He really is a samurai LOL</b>

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>That's Lupin III?</b>

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:27.840
<b>The world's greatest thief HA</b>

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:28.960
<b>Wasn't Lupin behind 
that thing a while back?</b>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.750
<b>Oh, I remember that!</b>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.750
<b>Where's Lupin going?</b>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:29.750
<b>I hear he has hideouts around the world.</b>

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.130
<b>The airport. He's obviously flying.</b>

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.470
<b>It's probably a group 
of 3 men and 1 woman.</b>

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.550
Some tickets were purchased 10 minutes ago
 for 3 men and 1 woman.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.850
They were headed for 
Dusseldorf on Berlin Air.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.300
I get it.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.090
So everyone in the world is a cop now, huh?

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.990
<b>The Lupin Game</b>

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:23.290
I guess this means we're
 celebrities now, huh?

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.580
There they are!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.260
It's the cops!

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.610
Lupin's over here!

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:30.880
Whoa, run for it!

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.850
I don't care! Get those patrol cars here now!

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.370
I'll take responsibility!

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:37.390
Hold on tight!

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:37.880
Right!

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:38.390
Left!

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:38.840
Right!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:39.370
Left!

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:39.740
Right!

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.320
Left!

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.000
Wall!

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:41.660
On it!

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:43.920
Left!

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:44.460
Right!

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:44.920
Left!

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:45.510
Right!

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.100
Left!

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.010
Amy, I need info on everywhere 
that's off-limits in this airport.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.020
It's Ami.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.150
Hello, Underworld.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.510
Spotter forum. The thread on airports.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.520
Since we're here, I figure we 
might as well steal a plane!

00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.870
Outta the way, people!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.110
The runway's through that door.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:02.490
They just went past me!!

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:02.490
Where'd Lupin go?

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:02.490
Where???

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.240
They're heading 
for the runway!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.400
Zenigata must've called for backup.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:14.470
What now?

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:15.830
Change of plan.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.170
Amy, what's the quickest 
way to a parking garage?

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.680
Lupin's in the western parking garage.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:27.340
Is he planning on stealing a car to escape?

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.180
Yata, we're heading back to the car!

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.570
Inspector, wait!

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.940
<b>I'd take the black one.</b>

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.940
<b>Hey, let's put bets on 
which one he'll take.</b>

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.940
<b>That's a thief for you.</b>

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.940
<b>He's gonna steal a car.</b>

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.940
<b>They're in the parking garage.</b>

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.960
What about this one, Lupin?

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:41.780
Nah.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:43.440
Let's take that one.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.790
Not your usual style.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.880
Did you finally started caring 
about the environment?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>Actually, it's the white car.</b>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>Where are they gonna go????</b>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>What's their endgame?</b>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>They left the 
parking garage.</b>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>It's the blue car.</b>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>Lupin's inside.</b>

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.710
<b>What's with
 that car?</b>

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.370
Lupin? You're not getting away!

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.380
<i>Stay where you are!</i>

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:07.070
We've got the airport on lockdown!

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.960
If you move now and clear the runway, 
you'll be playing right into Lupin's hands!

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.340
It's Zenigata.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:16.480
Where does a cop get off 
breaking the speed limit like that?

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.330
I told you we should've 
jacked the tough one.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:27.870
<b>The fuzz are pretty badass———</b>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:27.870
<b>Lupin's done for</b>

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:27.870
<b>Get him, popo!!</b>

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.120
<b>Lupin!! Behind you, dude!!</b>

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.370
<b>One more ram up the 
tailpipe oughta do it</b>

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.540
<b>Lupin's going down today!</b>

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:34.990
Got you!

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:47.760
Don't mess with me!

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:51.310
Goemon?!

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:59.430
There's nothing but the 
sea in that direction.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.800
He's trapped like a rat.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.920
No such luck. There's a special 
kind of aircraft in that hangar.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.930
What an odd-looking vehicle.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.790
It's an AW609.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.840
And those tiltrotors mean 
it doesn't need a runway.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.080
Impressive work, finding this baby.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:24.060
All I did was ask around on an 
internet forum about plane spotting.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.000
Hardly five minutes passed 
before I got a reply.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.230
No crowds or paparazzi in here, too.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.750
They've cut the damn power.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.280
Display scan of flight manual.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:47.210
The main engine needs 
electricity to start.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:48.020
Electricity?

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.790
And we've been cut off from the mains.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.820
Isn't fuel enough to get it in the air?

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:04.410
Most aircraft require a significant external 
source of electricity to start their engines.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.420
<b>They can't possibly 
get away now.</b>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.510
<b>Lupin kinda sucks</b>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.510
<b>Game over</b>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.510
<b>Wah, they're gonna 
get caught LOL</b>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.510
<b>They've gotta be 
out of options now</b>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.510
<b>That's that, then</b>

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.510
<b>Planes need electricity?</b>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:09.510
<b>Lupin's doomed</b>

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.510
<b>It's done</b>

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:10.930
<b>Kind of an anticlimax</b>

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:15.800
A samurai?

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.810
Is he bringing a sword to a gunfight?

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.150
Impossible! How did he...

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:38.240
He used the battery from the electric car?

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.390
Lupin!

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:40.710
He planned this all along!

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.250
Hop on, Goemon!

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.710
Lupin Game players, I bid you farewell.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.340
Don't think you've gotten away, Lupin.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:59.090
This is just the first round.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.680
<i>There it is! Look!</i>

00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:23.700
<i>We've found the plane Lupin used to escaped!</i>

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:27.650
There's a hundred million people 
playing the Lupin Game...

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.350
That's more than the 
entire population of France!

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:35.940
They were even talking about 
it on the radio earlier.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.430
We're dining with a superstar.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.790
You <i>do</i> know they're after you, too, right?

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:42.850
What?!

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.290
"Find Daisuke Jigen!"

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:48.850
"As Lupin's lover, wherever he goes,
 Lupin will be close by."

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:51.350
"Lover"?! Is that supposed to be a joke?!

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.860
Hey, don't back away!

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.040
Here.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:07:59.870
What?

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.860
Since we're having hot pot, 
you should join in the fun, Amy.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:07.360
It's Ami. And the two most important 
things in life are speed and data.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:13.880
From procuring the ingredients to washing 
the dishes, most meals take three hours.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:16.580
This, however, takes ten seconds.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.520
It's more nutritionally balanced, as well.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:23.750
If you break it down in terms of the 
amount of time it takes to get sustenance,

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.940
this is roughly 3,000% more efficient.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.970
Life itself is inefficient, my dear.

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.390
What the...

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.280
You guys are Japanese!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.160
Eat some of the tofu, would you?! Sheesh.

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.770
So what's the plan?

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.240
We gonna lie low for a bit?

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:44.680
No chance! I'm not just gonna take 
this kind of treatment lying down!

00:08:44.680 --> 00:08:47.050
Does that mean you have a plan?

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.870
You bet. An eye for an eye, as they say.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.160
Lupin's appeared online!

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:59.060
You've verified this?

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:01.450
Be careful you don't get taken in 
by some amateur's idea of a prank.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.170
No, sir, the thing is...

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.060
It's definitely him posting.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.940
The name's Lupin III! 
The world's greatest master thief!

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:17.290
I heard you guys are looking for me, 
so I've decided to grace you with my presence!

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:21.090
Excuse me, are you Lupin?

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:25.950
We're on our honeymoon and 
well... can I shake your hand?

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.870
Oh, you bet!

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:30.470
Want to take a picture together, too?

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.340
I even do autographs! What's your name?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.680
Robert? Where are you from, Robert?

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:36.040
You mean you <i>don't</i> write it in kanji?

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.220
Excuse me, Mr. Samurai.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.360
Would you mind taking a picture of us?

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.110
I just need to press this button, yes?

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.580
Ah. Thing is, Goemon, that's the dial 
for changing the shooting mode.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.050
And more importantly, 
you've got it the wrong way round.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.480
There you go. You've got it now.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.330
Let's go, Inspector!

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.620
What's the point?

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.360
To arrest him!

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.000
If we let him get away 
with showboating like this,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.590
it'll kill the ICPO's reputation stone dead!

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:07.820
Yata.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:11.630
Look closer at that picture. 
That ship's heading for Bwanda.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:19.680
And the Republic of Bwanda 
isn't an ICPO member nation.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:25.090
As long as he stays there, 
Lupin's out of our jurisdiction.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.020
<b>We made it to Bwanda!</b>

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.520
<b>Entering the country.</b>

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.020
<b>Bwandan taxis 
are so colorful!</b>

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.520
<b>At the front desk I</b>

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>At the front desk II</b>

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.400
<b>Nice and springy!</b>

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.940
<b>He's having a whale of a time~</b>

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.940
<b>Looks yummy</b>

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:37.940
<b>What dish is that?</b>

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.400
<b>Drinking in the afternoon, I'm jelly~</b>

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:39.410
<b>Where is this?</b>

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:44.630
What a cutie!

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.120
This country is full of beauties! Fantastic!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.120
<b>This country is full of beauties!! 
Fantastic!</b>

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.130
<b>Lupin III</b>

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.130
<b>starts a 
newsletter!</b>

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.130
<b>Click here 
for details</b>

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:56.660
Y'know, lately, it seems like my wife's 
besotted with another man...

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.700
It's like this guy is all she 
thinks about, 24 hours a day!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.680
So here's Lupin, who's supposedly 
being tracked by the whole world,

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.640
spamming people with 
info on where he is...

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:07.720
That should take all the fun out 
of trying to track me down,

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.630
and in time, people will get bored.

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:14.220
Once everyone's found a new toy, 
they'll forget all about little old me.

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:15.710
Is it really that simple?

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:19.310
People just don't care that 
much about other people.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.530
And in the meantime, 
we'll enjoy ourselves here!

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:36.770
That bastard Lupin... acting like 
he doesn't have a care in the world!

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:42.560
What do you mean?

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.300
<b>If we're talking internet expertise, 
<u>these guys are the real pros</u>.</b>

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:50.260
I get it.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:55.060
Time to sink everything 
we've got left into this.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:12:00.340
The Lupin Game seems to have come to an end.

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:04.510
Well, it's not much fun tracking someone 
down if they tell you where they are.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:09.310
People only enjoy the chase when 
they see someone running away...

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:12.340
Wouldn't you say you're 
the same, Fujiko Mine?

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.650
No lingering regrets regarding Lupin III?

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:19.010
I'm not sure what rumors you might've heard,

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:22.150
but Lupin and I are nothing more 
than professional acquaintances.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:44.790
Is that the Lupin Game?

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.550
It's kinda played out now.

00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:49.210
And that guy's always at 
the top of the rankings...

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.410
It'd be nice if something 
different happened for once.

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:53.200
Even if it did, it'd probably be a hoax.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:55.390
Who cares, as long as it's fun?

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.270
The problem is when it's boring!

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:04.490
Tonight's dinner is wild venison!

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:10.500
It's a shame I'm dining with this bearded 
old geezer instead of a beautiful lady, though.

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.390
Hey, don't drag me into this.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:18.010
Such frosty treatment! 
Aren't we supposed to be lovers?

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:20.750
Don't be weird!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:24.020
We're <i>coworkers,</i> that's all!

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:27.130
Would it have killed you 
to have said "friends"?

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:28.940
Oh! Here we go!

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:29.840
What is it?

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:33.000
Amy's finished doing the 
thing I asked her to do.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.960
<b>I uploaded it to 
Cloud Server 3.</b>

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.960
<b>Goodbye.</b>

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.590
Hey, now!

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:44.000
I've got a runaway to track down!

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:45.810
Good luck!

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.670
D'you know where you're goin', miss?

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.740
We can be your guides, if you like.

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:20.370
This will show me the way.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:23.870
We know some good spots that 
aren't marked on there.

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:25.390
You should come with us.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:28.550
Why wouldn't they be on the internet?

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.880
Are they brand new?

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.970
Are they "members only"? Or maybe illegal?

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.340
Shut up! They're—

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:36.270
There are no such spots.

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.300
Who said that?!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:44.440
Run along, old man. They don't allow anyone over 30.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:46.740
Hey, that's Lupin III!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.980
Lupin? The guy from that internet game?

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:52.450
Don't think you're a big deal 
just because you're a celeb!

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:58.940
Don't mess with us!

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:07.000
We're not done—

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.970
You shouldn't mess with grownups, boys.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.890
I'm Lupin III. And I'm not some 
entertainer you watch on TV.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:15.960
I'm a thief.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:19.230
And that means, sometimes, I steal lives.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.850
If you're not prepared to follow through,

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.370
don't even start.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.230
Why'd you come after me?

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:44.150
I should be asking the questions here.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:46.010
Saying goodbye out of the blue like that...

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:51.130
You spirited me away. I gave you 
backdoor access to Marco Polo.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.890
Our business is concluded. 
There's no reason for us to stay together.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:59.020
I take good care of the things I steal.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:03.210
That's not true. I saw some 
of your loot at the villa.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:05.670
It didn't look like you 
were taking care of it.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:08.790
Pretty observant when you wanna be...

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:12.980
Why didn't you leave me at 
the airport in France?

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:15.320
Well... it just kinda happened that way?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.280
Then, why do you let me 
stay in your hotel room?

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:18.920
I asked you to do a job for me.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.310
There are others hackers you could've asked.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.380
From what you've said to me,

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:29.050
I can only surmise that you 
want me to accompany you.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:33.670
Y'know, inductive reasoning 
can only throw up theories...

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:35.490
So I dug deeper.

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:39.880
I've been implanted with a tracking device.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:41.440
Who did that?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:45.950
Someone who knew my location 
and came after me.

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:46.960
In other words...

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.390
And that's why you wanted to leave?

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.230
It was the most expedient 
and logical thing to do.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:59.390
Conclusion: you're protecting me. Why?

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:05.730
Well, you know... "Unspoken words 
are the flowers of silence."

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:06.770
Flowers?

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.680
It's a Japanese saying.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:11.000
Hello, Underworld.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.370
You don't have to look it up.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:15.900
What I'm trying to say...

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:18.180
Well, it wouldn't be cool if 
I just came out and said it.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:23.440
Do you want to have sex with me, Lupin?

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:25.940
No!

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.850
That's not it at all...

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:37.810
If I left you by yourself, 
Marco Polo would come after you.

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:40.850
I just wanna keep you safe 
until things calm down...

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:43.450
Man, explaining is lame!

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:47.950
I still don't understand.

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:50.740
I don't think I do anymore, either.

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:04.440
Speak of the devil. Looks like 
Marco Polo have made their move.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:08.430
Bringing in the hitmen... Pretty simple
approach for a bunch of tech wizards.

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:13.460
He posts the hotels and restaurants he visits...

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:16.160
He even says when he's taking a bath,
 and when he's going to bed.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:20.920
You'd be hard-pressed to find a target 
who makes it easier to track them down.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:23.970
Let's take that truck.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.040
You're... Shinpei Mayama?

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.400
I recognize you.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:42.850
Not your face, but your 
M.O. is pretty infamous.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:43.810
The Flea.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:47.450
This is gonna be tough to handle solo...

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:09.500
Very impressive, Goemon.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:11.820
You people are with the Union...

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:22.170
Captain Bone and Guardsman?

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:25.690
It's like the assassin 
all-stars are out tonight.

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:30.930
In other words, it's a betting pool where 
gamblers bet on when people will die.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:33.100
It'd be one thing if they 
were terminally ill,

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:36.300
but there's no sense in trying to 
guess when someone will die.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.660
There are ways to <i>force</i> the issue, though.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:41.900
Are you suggesting...

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.550
If you were to kill them on 
the day you'd put your bet on...

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:49.170
it would count as a correct guess.

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:58.070
This website accepts digital 
currency, which can't be traced.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:03.430
The people placing the bets and the people 
guessing are protected by anonymous browsing.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.970
All anyone did was guess 
what day Lupin would die.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.680
Which is perfectly legal.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:11.060
No one said anything 
about killing him.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:16.200
It's a game totally free 
of danger, Lupin III.

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.080
<b>I've never seen assassins before.</b>

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.080
<b>Wow, they're real.</b>

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.080
<b>Are we gonna see someone die?</b>

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.580
<b>Things are heating up!</b>

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:36.070
Amy, get behind me.

00:20:39.200 --> 00:20:41.610
And don't even <i>think</i> about thanking me.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:43.690
See, I'm protecting you...

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.010
...because I love being the 
kind of guy who does that.

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:17.800
The name's Daisuke Jigen.

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:22.650
We've got the assassin all-stars from 
all over the world on our tails.

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:28.270
Apparently, there's a new game on the 
internet, and this one involves killing us.

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:29.660
<b>Vacation 
Request</b>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.260
I guess the internet can be a real 
pain if you get on its bad side.

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:36.950
So what now, Lupin? You got a plan?

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.580
Next time: "The Killers 
Gather in the Wasteland."

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:44.950
<b>The Killers Gather in the Wasteland</b>

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:44.120
Might be a good chance to deal 
with them all at once...
